{{ contract }}

`src/env.js` must export:
- `export function buildEnv(THREE, scene) → env` where `env = { sun, ambient, sky, ground, water, fog, heightAt }`
  (fields may be null when absent). It adds sky (a large inverted sphere or a gradient ShaderMaterial
  dome), the key light (`THREE.DirectionalLight` placed along the planned azimuth/elevation at ≥ 0.6 ×
  the bounds' extent, `castShadow` with a shadow camera covering the bounds), an ambient/hemisphere
  light, scene fog (`THREE.Fog` or `FogExp2` with the planned colour/density), the ground (plane or
  subdivided terrain covering the bounds), and water if planned.
- `export function heightAt(x, z) → y` (terrain height; 0 for flat ground). Zones call it to place
  assets on the ground — it must be deterministic and cheap.
- `export const MATS = { ... }` a small registry of shared `MeshStandardMaterial`s (stone, wood, leaf,
  water, metal …) with hex colours so zones look coherent.
- `export function tickEnv(t, dt) {}` for animated sky/water/fog (may be empty).

## DO
- Use the planned numbers literally: sun azimuth/elevation → `sun.position.set(cos(el)*sin(az), sin(el), cos(el)*cos(az)) * R`.
- Colour-manage: `renderer.outputColorSpace` is set by the harness; author colours as sRGB hex.
- Make it read at the planned time of day in ONE frame: exposure via light intensities (sun 1.5-3.0
  at noon, 0.3-0.8 at dusk with warm colour; ambient 0.2-0.6).
- Keep the whole module ≤ 250 lines; no textures, no DOM, no fetch.

## DON'T
- No assets/zones here (they come from other modules). No cameras. No `scene.background` image loads.

